  "id": "color-perception",
  "term": "color perception",
  "definition": "Color perception is the brain’s processing of color signals from the eyes in the visual cortex, turning them into meaningful representations. It depends on many neurons and is shaped not just by the wavelengths coming from an object, but also by surrounding colors and brightness contrast at its edges.",
